      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture of what to improve. The `test_Chronology_range` method is a flat list of 13 assertions with no grouping, no explanation of the 4-argument `ValueRange.of` semantics, and the class carries unused data-provider methods that add noise. I'll:\n1. Remove the unused data-provider methods and their imports\n2. Add a comment explaining the `ValueRange.of(smallestMin, largestMin, smallestMax, largestMax)` contract\n3. Group assertions by semantic category with explanatory inline commentsThe improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes unused data-provider methods, trims imports to only what's needed, and organizes the 13 assertions into four labeled groups (week-alignment fields, day fields, epoch day, month fields, year/era fields) with comments explaining the Discordian-specific semantics — particularly why `ValueRange` minimums can be 0 (St. Tib's Day)."
